WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.320
While the Cold War with the Soviet&nbsp;
Union was a nuclear arms race,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.160
the Cold War with China is&nbsp;
being fought in digital space.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.600
In late August, Washington restricted&nbsp;
sales of sophisticated chips&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.520
to China and Russia. (August 26 - informed NVIDIA)

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:21.040
The two top Silicon Valley chip designers,&nbsp;
NVIDIA and Advanced Micro Devices, have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.960
told to limit sales of their high-end chips&nbsp;
known as graphics processing units or GPUs.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.080
GPUs were originally developed&nbsp;
to render images in video games&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:38.160
but are now used in supercomputers that recognize&nbsp;
speech and identify objects in photographs.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.160
In other words, they can be used for&nbsp;
artificial intelligence gathering.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.320
The People’s Daily, the mouthpiece&nbsp;
of China’s Communist Party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.200
claimed on its Twitter account that the country’s&nbsp;
facial recognition system could scan the faces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:58.720
of China’s 1.4 billion citizens in just one&nbsp;
second. And by the way, this tweet was in 2018.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:05.600
NVIDIA, the largest GPU maker by far, confirmed&nbsp;
that the U.S. federal government now requires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.480
the company to seek export licenses&nbsp;
to sell two types of high-end chips:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:16.320
the A100 and the upcoming H100, and any&nbsp;
future chips equivalent in performance.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:16.880
For AMD, the affected chip is the MI250.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:22.880
These processors help “accelerate” the most&nbsp;
intensive parts of machine learning used in AI.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.160
In an SEC filing, NVIDIA revealed that&nbsp;
the U.S. government fears there is a risk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:34.720
that the products “may be used in or diverted&nbsp;
to a “military end use” in China and Russia.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.120
Both companies do not currently sell to Russia.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.880
NVIDIA’s statement indicates it does not&nbsp;
expect licenses to be granted in most cases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.400
and could take a $400 million&nbsp;
dollar hit this quarter.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.040
Beijing is clearly not happy&nbsp;
about the restrictions.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.960
A Chinese foreign ministry official said the U.S.&nbsp;
is trying to impose a “technological blockade” on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:02.800
China and that the restrictions show America is&nbsp;
trying to maintain its “technological hegemony”.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.120
Reuters quoted the U.S. Department of Commerce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.680
as saying the restrictions are meant to "keep&nbsp;
advanced technologies out of the wrong hands.”

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.360
These restrictions come shortly after the Biden&nbsp;
administration offered billions in subsidies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:21.840
to a Taiwanese company IF it agrees not to sell&nbsp;
its most advanced semiconductor chips to China.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:26.080
Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing&nbsp;
Company makes the most advanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.480
chips for nearly every company on&nbsp;
earth, including Nvidia and AMD.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.200
Although TSMC has factories&nbsp;
in China and one in the U.S.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.760
its most advanced factories are in&nbsp;
Taiwan…for security reasons. I did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.760
a story about the importance of TSMC&nbsp;
which I’ll link in my description.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:50.640
TSMC is now building a $12 billion dollar&nbsp;
factory in Arizona so it’s no surprise that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:56.320
Arizona’s governor Doug Ducey is the latest&nbsp;
American politician to cozy up to Taiwan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.440
He flew there to meet with&nbsp;
Taiwanese President Tsai Ing-wen.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:00.160
Chinese firms are making their own semiconductor&nbsp;
chips, though they are a generation or two

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.000
Not to mention in 2019, the&nbsp;
Trump administration lobbied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.280
the Dutch government to block the&nbsp;
shipment of cutting-edge machines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:12.400
that are an essential component in printing&nbsp;
chips for TSMC and other chipmakers.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:18.720
The Dutch firm ASML is the only company in the&nbsp;
world making the $150 million dollar machines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.480
that pattern the finest lines&nbsp;
on the most advanced chips.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:28.320
The Biden administration has been pushing ASML to&nbsp;
stop shipping even its less sophisticated systems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.440
to China, which would seriously hurt Chinese firms&nbsp;
that are producing their own semiconductor chips.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.680
These new U.S. restrictions&nbsp;
involving Nvidia and AMD&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.000
are another attempt to hamper&nbsp;
China’s technological capabilities.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.920
Without integrated units from those&nbsp;
two companies, Chinese firms will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:50.480
find it more difficult to implement advanced&nbsp;
computing for speech and image recognition.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.080
These processors are commonly&nbsp;
found in smartphones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.880
for example, to identify people in photos.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:00.320
However, they also have military uses.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.720
Such as scouring satellite imagery&nbsp;
for weapons or military bases.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:09.840
Or listening to communications and monitoring&nbsp;
faces for intelligence-gathering purposes.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.160
Washington has argued that products&nbsp;
sold in the Chinese marketplace are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.280
ending up in the hands of the Chinese military.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:22.000
For example, Nvidia and Intel sold&nbsp;
chips to Sugon, a Chinese firm that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.120
makes computers for various companies but&nbsp;
also supplies them to the Chinese military.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:32.080
A report in 2020 by the New York Times&nbsp;
raised concerns that these chips are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:36.320
powering a supercomputing center that&nbsp;
conducts mass surveillance in China’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:41.840
northwestern Xinjiang province to track&nbsp;
Uighurs and other Muslim minorities.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.080
Both Intel and Nvidia told the Times&nbsp;
they were unaware of what they called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.000
the misuse of their technology.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:55.120
In 2016, a Chinese police surveillance project&nbsp;
called Sharp Eyes had the ambitious plan of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:02.480
being able to monitor 100% of all public spaces&nbsp;
in China by 2020 - even the vast rural areas.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.680
There is no word on how far they’ve&nbsp;
come in achieving this goal.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.440
Although the blockade is meant&nbsp;
to prevent American technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:14.960
from being used by America’s military&nbsp;
rival, AI chips have wide applications.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.800
Companies like Alibaba,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:22.240
Baidu, and Tencent use them in their data&nbsp;
centers to process large volumes of data.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:27.600
Now, they’ll have to make do with&nbsp;
lower-performance GPUs that could slow them down.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.960
So, there are broader implications for society.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:36.640
Or, perhaps, it is inevitable that&nbsp;
China will begin producing its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.000
high-end GPUs and become self-reliant.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.760
It may only be a matter of time.

